# Gates that must distinguish clean, findings, and inconclusive.
#
# check-gates-are-honest.sh drives every gate listed here against three fixtures
# and requires it to be distinguished across all three: exit 0 on a clean
# subject, exit 1 on one with a real problem, exit 2 on one it cannot look at.
#
#   <subject-kind> <gate-command>
#
# The subject kind selects a fixture builder, and a kind with no builder is a
# finding rather than something to skip. Adding a gate means choosing one, which
# means answering "what does this look at, and what does it look like when there
# is nothing?" -- the question that produces the bug this file exists to catch.
#
# Kinds available today:
#   git-tree       the gate audits a git work tree          (empty = nothing tracked)
#   workflow-dir   the gate audits a .github/workflows tree (empty = no workflows)
#
# Paths are relative to the repository root, and the gate must be executable.

git-tree       scripts/check-home-paths.sh
workflow-dir   scripts/check-workflows-can-fail.sh
